.SH NAME
lmm-version - Show lmm's version and whether a newer release exists


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlmm version [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the running lmm version, the newest lmm release it knows of, and how
this binary was installed - which is how to upgrade it.

.PP
lmm checks GitHub for a new release at most once a day, after an interactive
command (and while 'lmm serve' runs), and remembers the answer. 'lmm version'
reports that remembered answer; --check asks GitHub now, even when the
automatic check is turned off with 'update_check: false' in config.yaml.

.PP
Examples:
  lmm version
  lmm version --check
  lmm version --check --json


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--check\fP[=false]
	ask GitHub for the latest release now

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for version


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	config directory (default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lmm or ~/.config/lmm)

.PP
\fB--data\fP=""
	data directory (default: $XDG_DATA_HOME/lmm or ~/.local/share/lmm)

.PP
\fB-g\fP, \fB--game\fP=""
	game ID to operate on

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	output JSON instead of text; mutating commands print their result, --dry-run prints the plan; never prompts

.PP
\fB--log-level\fP="off"
	diagnostic log level written to stderr (off, error, warn, info, debug)

.PP
